# id  tag  kind  t_s  alt_km  L_si_W  flag  note
1 - first_light 0.0030 100.000 4.0268e+05 info  L_si first exceeds 1e-6 of its peak. This is just a visibility threshold; the real value depends on your sensor floor and on where the simulation starts (zstart).
2 A ablation_onset 5.3040 77.534 1.9580e+07 stylized  Net heating flux first exceeds radiative loss at T_ablate = 2300 K, so ablation switches on (a kink in the slope). Real onset is gradual over a few km. BELOW this point the model's light is drag work only (no ablated material): treat light above ~78 km as low-confidence. Loosely like the end of Phase 1 / start of Phase 2 in [R22], but the model has no spin, volatile (Na/K) emission or melt physics.
3 Y first_yield 13.0200 45.520 2.3622e+09 physical  Loading rho v^2 reaches S0 = 0.3 MPa. The body starts to flatten (pancake): area, drag and heating all grow, so the light rises faster. Analogue of the onset of fragmentation (Phase 5 / H_f in [R22]).
4 - drag_overtakes_ablation 13.0230 45.508 2.3661e+09 stylized  Drag work now exceeds the kinetic energy carried off by ablated mass. The ratio ablation/drag is about Lambda v^2/(2 Q Cd), so this happens when the speed falls below ~14 km/s (from the model's heating law).
5 F flare 13.2005 44.783 6.9340e+09 stylized  Light rises x45.0 in 0.43 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: yield gen 0 at 45.5 km (99% of m0); split gen 0 at 44.1 km (99% of m0). Dust groups supply 93% of the rise and 91% of the light at the end of the flare (the model releases dust all at once, so a dust-dominated first flare is by construction). A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
6 B first_breakup 13.3620 44.124 1.4651e+10 stylized  Spread factor reached f_split = 2: the body breaks into 4 children plus 20 % of its mass as dust. The dust has a large area-to-mass ratio, decelerates and ablates within a fraction of a second, which makes a sharp flare. The instantaneous release is a model simplification. Light grew x6.2 between first yield and this breakup (pancake spreading).
7 F flare 14.0680 41.345 1.2494e+11 stylized  Light rises x1.3 in 0.09 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: split gen 1 at 41.3 km (37% of m0). Dust groups supply 100% of the rise and 77% of the light at the end of the flare (the model releases dust all at once, so a dust-dominated first flare is by construction). A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
8 b bump 14.4530 39.866 1.2269e+11 stylized  Small fluctuation, 5% above the local trend; coincides with a split (gen 1) at 39.8 km. The fine structure of this phase is set by the cascade rules, so its pattern is not predictive of a real event.
9 b bump 14.8630 38.276 1.6491e+11 stylized  Small fluctuation, 16% above the local trend; coincides with a split (gen 2) at 38.2 km. The fine structure of this phase is set by the cascade rules, so its pattern is not predictive of a real event.
10 P peak 14.8650 38.269 1.6493e+11 physical  Maximum light. It sits ~+0.5 km from the peak of energy deposition (37.8 km) because the luminous efficiency tau(v) falls as the fragments slow (mass-weighted speed here 11.2 km/s).
11 b bump 15.2980 36.725 1.2555e+11 stylized  Small fluctuation, 5% above the local trend; coincides with a split (gen 2) at 36.4 km. The fine structure of this phase is set by the cascade rules, so its pattern is not predictive of a real event.
12 b bump 15.8530 34.852 8.5650e+10 stylized  Small fluctuation, 5% above the local trend; no breakup within 0.1 s (overlap of several groups' light / pancake growth). The fine structure of this phase is set by the cascade rules, so its pattern is not predictive of a real event.
13 D rolloff 16.1130 34.089 6.0512e+10 physical  Light has fallen to 1/e of the peak 1.25 s after it. Cause: the kinetic energy is being used up (speed 62% of v0, 61% of the mass still in flight) and tau(v) drops with speed. Analogue of Phase 7 (decline until dark flight) in [R22].
14 T tail 19.4520 25.637 1.6435e+08 low-confidence  Below 1e-3 of the peak the light is controlled by groups being retired when they slow below v_dark = 3.0 km/s and by the tau taper (2-4 km/s). Do not interpret structure below this level.
